From 16c2bf5c7633199f1b8dce4bcb5af6f743fadb27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:51:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(browser): vet every request against DNS-aware SSRF policy

A navigation preflight already resolved the hostname, but subresources and
redirect hops reached the server-side Chromium without a DNS check, and an
IPv4-mapped dotted-quad answer (e.g. ::ffff:10.0.0.1) slipped past the IPv6
policy because the trailing dotted-quad was mis-folded into four hex groups.

- Attach a Playwright route handler (attachRequestGuards) that resolves every
  request URL with dns.lookup(all) and aborts it if any address is private /
  loopback / link-local / CGNAT / IPv4-mapped, covering subresources and each
  redirect hop beyond the navigation preflight.
- Fix expandIpv6 dotted-quad folding to combine octets into two 16-bit groups
  so raw DNS mapped answers are classified correctly.
- Keep the post-load final-URL recheck; unit tests stub the resolver for
  public, private, mixed, metadata, CGNAT, and IPv6-mapped answers and drive
  the route handler through the fake page, with no network.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
